  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="21">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> 21</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="381" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif man cirican nydþeowige, gebete þæt be lahslihte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="306" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif man cirican nydþeowige, gebete þæt be lahslihte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="381" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand eine Kirche verknechtet, büsse er das durch Rechtsbruchbusse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone forcibly enslaves a church, let him atone for it with the fine for breach of law (lahslit).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="482" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone brings a church under subjection, he is to pay compensation with <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="307" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone compels service from a church, he is to compensate for that with <hi rend="italic">lahslit</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="381"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_15">VI Atr 15</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 15.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
